WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:05.390
Netflix puts billions of dollars into new
content every year, but while everyone hears

00:00:05.390 --> 00:00:10.310
about buzzy releases like Orange Is the New
Black and House of Cards, the sheer amount

00:00:10.310 --> 00:00:13.510
of content means other shows get lost in the
shuffle.

00:00:13.510 --> 00:00:17.480
To help out, here are a bunch of upcoming
Netflix originals that are going to blow you

00:00:17.480 --> 00:00:18.060
away.

00:00:18.780 --> 00:00:19.500
Disjointed

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:25.000
Kathy Bates is getting high for Disjointed,
a comedy in which she stars as Ruth, "a woman

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:28.710
whose lifelong mission has been to decriminalize
marijuana."

00:00:28.710 --> 00:00:34.329
The series finds Ruth running a Los Angeles-area
marijuana dispensary—and finding that business

00:00:34.329 --> 00:00:36.400
is much, much harder when you're stoned.

00:00:36.820 --> 00:00:42.140
Disjointed, which released a teaser on 4/20,
will premiere its 20-episode first season

00:00:42.160 --> 00:00:43.420
on August 25th.

00:00:43.900 --> 00:00:49.269
David Javerbaum of The Daily Show co-created
the comedy alongside Chuck Lorre, and a strong

00:00:49.269 --> 00:00:51.640
supporting cast rounds out the ensemble.

00:00:52.260 --> 00:00:53.180
Hold the Dark

00:00:53.700 --> 00:00:58.920
Adapted from the William Giraldi 2014 novel
of the same name, Hold the Dark focuses on

00:00:58.929 --> 00:01:03.879
the pursuit of a wolf responsible for killing
children in the Alaskan wilderness, and stars

00:01:03.880 --> 00:01:06.940
Alexander Skarsgard and Westworld's Jeffrey
Wright

00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:12.230
Hold the Dark comes from director Jeremy Saulnier,
the man behind the critically acclaimed thriller

00:01:12.230 --> 00:01:13.040
Green Room.

00:01:13.300 --> 00:01:18.980
While Hold the Dark doesn't yet have a release
date, it started production in early 2017,

00:01:18.980 --> 00:01:22.140
so hopefully Saulnier will be back to terrify
viewers soon.

00:01:22.680 --> 00:01:23.680
Green Eggs and Ham

00:01:24.240 --> 00:01:29.060
Netflix's adaptation of Dr. Seuss' Green Eggs
and Ham will follow the book's characters

00:01:29.060 --> 00:01:32.800
Guy and Sam as they "take a road trip to save
an endangered animal."

00:01:33.040 --> 00:01:37.260
Along the way, they learn about friendship—and,
of course, green eggs and ham.

00:01:37.580 --> 00:01:42.280
Ellen DeGeneres' attachment as an executive
producer is already a great sign for Green

00:01:42.280 --> 00:01:48.620
Eggs and Ham, which, despite the book's popularity,
has yet to be adapted into a film or TV series,

00:01:48.810 --> 00:01:52.780
aside from the 1973 special Dr. Seuss on the
Loose.

00:01:52.780 --> 00:01:57.310
Netflix has stayed pretty quiet about the
show since greenlighting it in 2015, but their

00:01:57.310 --> 00:02:02.620
website notes that its 13-episode first season
is expected to debut in 2018.

00:02:03.740 --> 00:02:04.620
The Irishman

00:02:05.340 --> 00:02:10.879
With an estimated budget of over $100 million,
The Irishman is one of Netflix's priciest

00:02:10.879 --> 00:02:16.389
upcoming projects, but one that's definitely
worth the price—it reunites Martin Scorsese

00:02:16.389 --> 00:02:21.579
with Robert De Niro, along with a rumored
supporting cast of heavy hitters like Al Pacino,

00:02:21.580 --> 00:02:23.840
Joe Pesci, and Harvey Keitel.

00:02:24.110 --> 00:02:29.680
The Irishman stars De Niro as Frank "The Irishman"
Sheeran, the mob hitman allegedly responsible

00:02:29.689 --> 00:02:31.209
for the death of Jimmy Hoffa.

00:02:31.209 --> 00:02:33.300
"It's about Hoffa, um.

00:02:34.660 --> 00:02:37.880
Basically it's the guy confesses that he had
killed Hoffa."

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:42.960
With a huge amount of talent on both sides
of the camera, this movie will surely be on

00:02:42.960 --> 00:02:45.140
your radar—and in your queue—soon.

00:02:45.480 --> 00:02:46.560
Lost in Space

00:02:46.980 --> 00:02:51.650
Netflix is setting out to remake the popular
1960s series Lost in Space,.

00:02:51.650 --> 00:02:53.100
You know, this one:

00:02:53.580 --> 00:02:54.100
"It crashed over there.

00:02:54.760 --> 00:02:55.840
Come on, let's take a look."

00:02:56.120 --> 00:02:57.460
"Danger, Will Robinson.

00:02:57.460 --> 00:02:57.960
Danger."

00:02:58.620 --> 00:03:03.420
The show will follow a new cast on the spaceship
Jupiter 2, which is stranded light years away

00:03:03.420 --> 00:03:06.060
from its original destination after a crash.

00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:11.000
Cast member Toby Stephens calls it a "very
clever, modern reworking" of the original

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:11.940
show's story.

00:03:12.220 --> 00:03:15.520
The 10-episode reboot is expected out in 2018.

00:03:16.180 --> 00:03:16.980
Little Evil

00:03:17.640 --> 00:03:23.279
This horror comedy stars Adam Scott and Evangeline
Lilly as a newly married couple with a son...

00:03:23.280 --> 00:03:25.200
who just might be the Antichrist.

00:03:25.500 --> 00:03:30.180
In addition to a fun premise and a great cast,
Little Evil has some impressive people working

00:03:30.180 --> 00:03:35.689
behind the scenes, with Tucker and Dale vs.
Evil writer/director Eli Craig once again

00:03:35.689 --> 00:03:40.079
pulling double duty for his first feature
since that 2010 cult hit.

00:03:40.080 --> 00:03:42.820
The movie is expected to debut in 2017.

00:03:43.560 --> 00:03:44.360
Mute

00:03:44.980 --> 00:03:48.760
Hold the Dark isn't Alexander Skarsgard's
only upcoming Netflix film.

00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:50.540
He'll also star in Mute.

00:03:50.900 --> 00:03:56.240
Skarsgard plays Leo, a mute bartender living
in a near-future Berlin who embarks on a mission

00:03:56.240 --> 00:03:59.800
through the city's seedy underbelly to try
and find his missing girlfriend.

00:04:00.240 --> 00:04:05.240
Mute is the second film in a sci-fi trilogy
from director Duncan Jones, who says it's

00:04:05.240 --> 00:04:09.140
set in the same universe as his 2009 cult
favorite Moon.

00:04:09.400 --> 00:04:14.180
Jones says he plans for Mute to imagine Berlin
the way Blade Runner depicted Los Angeles—just

00:04:14.180 --> 00:04:18.620
one more reason it'll definitely be one to
watch when it debuts later this year.

00:04:19.320 --> 00:04:20.400
Game Over, Man!

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:25.820
The Workaholics gang will reunite for Game
Over, Man!, an action comedy featuring Blake

00:04:25.820 --> 00:04:30.820
Anderson, Anders Holm, and Adam Devine as
three friends "on the verge of getting their

00:04:30.820 --> 00:04:35.060
video game financed when their benefactor
is taken hostage by terrorists."

00:04:35.060 --> 00:04:40.540
Seth Rogen is set to produce the film alongside
his writing partner Evan Goldberg, and Kyle

00:04:40.540 --> 00:04:44.900
Newacheck, the co-creator of Workaholics,
will direct based on a script from Anders

00:04:44.900 --> 00:04:45.400
Holm.

00:04:46.280 --> 00:04:46.900
IO

00:04:47.700 --> 00:04:53.260
This sci-fi movie tells the story of Sam Walde,
a teen who finds herself one of the few survivors

00:04:53.260 --> 00:04:54.860
on a post-apocalyptic Earth.

00:04:55.110 --> 00:04:59.800
Sam is played by The Nice Guys' Margaret Qualley,
and Anthony Mackie—who you'll recognize

00:04:59.810 --> 00:05:05.370
as The Avengers' Falcon—co-stars as Micah,
a fellow refugee on his way to the last human

00:05:05.370 --> 00:05:06.620
shuttle leaving Earth.

00:05:06.900 --> 00:05:12.180
Danny Huston, recently spotted in DC's Wonder
Woman, will also appear in an undisclosed

00:05:12.180 --> 00:05:12.680
role.

00:05:12.840 --> 00:05:17.120
There's no word yet on when the movie will
premiere, although filming took place in late

00:05:17.120 --> 00:05:21.520
2016, so hopefully IO will be here to get
all of our hearts racing soon.

00:05:22.200 --> 00:05:22.860
Big Mouth

00:05:23.640 --> 00:05:28.800
Netflix's upcoming animated comedy Big Mouth
follows comedian Nick Kroll's time as an awkward

00:05:28.800 --> 00:05:34.060
teenager growing up with his best friend Andrew
Goldberg, now a writer and producer for Family

00:05:34.060 --> 00:05:34.560
Guy.

00:05:34.560 --> 00:05:38.760
Kroll voices himself, with fellow standup
John Mulaney playing Goldberg.

00:05:38.980 --> 00:05:43.640
Kroll calls the show "over 30 years in the
making," and he's clearly using his comedy

00:05:43.650 --> 00:05:49.530
connections to round out the cast—he's recruited
an impressive roster that includes Maya Rudolph,

00:05:49.530 --> 00:05:53.210
Jordan Peele, Fred Armisen, and Jenny Slate.

00:05:53.210 --> 00:05:55.740
The series is expected out in 2017.

00:05:56.440 --> 00:05:57.440
Gerald's Game

00:05:58.040 --> 00:06:03.420
There are about a billion Stephen King adaptations
in the works, and Netflix is joining the arena

00:06:03.420 --> 00:06:08.940
with Gerald's Game, starring Watchmen's Carla
Gugino as a woman stranded in her lakeside

00:06:08.940 --> 00:06:11.390
home after a sex game gone wrong.

00:06:11.390 --> 00:06:15.390
Gerald's Game doesn't have a release date
yet, but it boasts an accomplished horror

00:06:15.390 --> 00:06:16.840
director in Mike Flanagan.

00:06:17.260 --> 00:06:22.580
Flanagan also has King's full support—Gugino
has said that King was a big fan of Flanagan's

00:06:22.580 --> 00:06:25.560
Hush and gave him his blessing in pursuing
the project.

00:06:25.800 --> 00:06:30.460
King is also apparently pretty happy with
the early cut, tweeting in February of this

00:06:30.460 --> 00:06:33.640
year that the movie is "horrifying, hypnotic,
terrific."

00:06:34.120 --> 00:06:35.420
1922

00:06:35.780 --> 00:06:41.800
Another Stephen King adaptation in the works
at Netflix, 1922 stars an actor familiar with

00:06:41.800 --> 00:06:47.360
the bestselling author's work: Thomas Jane,
who led the 2003 film adaptation of King's

00:06:47.360 --> 00:06:51.590
Dreamcatcher and the 2007 adaptation of The
Mist.

00:06:51.590 --> 00:06:56.300
Jane plays Wilfred James, a man who admits
to killing his wife with the help of his teenage

00:06:56.300 --> 00:06:56.800
son.

00:06:56.880 --> 00:06:59.820
After her death, he starts to believe that
she's haunting him.

00:07:00.520 --> 00:07:01.560
Altered Carbon

00:07:02.080 --> 00:07:07.800
Based on the 2002 novel by Richard K. Morgan,
Altered Carbon focuses on Takeshi Kovacs,

00:07:07.800 --> 00:07:12.860
a former elite warrior who's been imprisoned
for 500 years before his mind is downloaded

00:07:12.860 --> 00:07:14.940
into someone else's body to solve a murder.

00:07:15.140 --> 00:07:19.940
Suicide Squad star Joel Kinnaman will take
on the role of Kovacs, starring opposite Kristin

00:07:19.940 --> 00:07:21.860
Lehman and James Purefoy.

00:07:22.420 --> 00:07:23.560
Thanks for watching!

00:07:23.560 --> 00:07:26.360
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:07:26.360 --> 00:07:28.780
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

